.TH DENIAL-SESSION 1 "August 2026" "Denial" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
denial-session \- start or validate an installed Denial desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B denial-session
.RI [ \-\-check ]
.br
.B denial-session
.RI [ deniald-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B denial-session
is the supported entry point for an installed Denial graphical session. It
resolves the display and optional render devices by capability, initializes
and validates the user's output configuration, locates the packaged Flutter
bundle, discovers an available user-session lifecycle, and starts
.BR deniald (1).
.PP
Display-manager session entries invoke this command directly. On systems with
an active systemd user manager, Denial activates its packaged
.B denial-session.target
after the compositor has published its endpoints and completed initial KMS
presentation. On other logind-compatible systems the launcher process owns
the compositor lifecycle directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the compositor, control client, session lifecycle, Flutter bundle,
output configuration, DRM selection, renderer, and Xwayland without starting
a compositor.
.TP
.B \-\-start-locked
Start with Denial's native authentication gate locked. Use this for direct or
autologin sessions that were not authenticated by a display manager.
.PP
All other arguments are forwarded to
.BR deniald (1).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I /etc/denial/session.conf
Root-owned shell-compatible machine configuration. Supported overrides include
.BR DENIAL_DRM_DEVICE ,
.BR DENIAL_RENDER_DEVICE ,
.BR DENIA_SHELL_PROFILE ,
.BR DENIA_FLUTTER_RENDERER ,
and
.BR DENIAL_FLUTTER_BUNDLE .
.TP
.I /etc/denial/outputs.conf
System output template copied to a user's configuration on first launch.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/denial/outputs.conf
Per-user persistent output configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/denial-session.target
Packaged graphical-session target used when a systemd user manager is
available.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that validation succeeded or that the compositor exited
normally. Installation, configuration, device-discovery, and compositor
failures return nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deniald (1),
.BR denialctl (1)
